WEBVTT

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.140
I wonder why...

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.220
The ceiling seems so familiar.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.300
To begin with, the only ceiling
I've looked at in three years is my cell's.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:51.640
Where am I?

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.180
Good morning.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.050
You're up early today.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.510
Hey, you're supposed to knock!

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:10.930
I'm still sleeping.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.930
Good morning.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:14.680
That's some bedhead.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.350
Come on. Five more minutes. Go away.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:20.640
Too bright!

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.300
What's wrong?

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.550
It's our daughter.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.100
It's not Kaeru.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.550
It's my actual--

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:28.760
Wait.

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.050
I'm not Sakaido.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:35.930
I'm Narihisago Akihito.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.260
I'm myself.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.600
But I remember.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:44.300
Kaeru. The Mizuhanome. The Kura.
The cases and serial killers. My killings.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.930
And how I got here, too.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:49.850
I remember it all.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.760
After ten minutes, push eject.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.510
Only two minutes?!

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.260
Aki?

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.140
Hey, close the door.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.550
What's going on?

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:07.430
What's wrong, Aki?

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:10.180
Hey, get a room!

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:17.970
Must have been one strange dream you had.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.470
Which means, this must be a world

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:29.800
created by a fictitious Mizuhanome
within the Mizuhanome. A total fabrication.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:35.100
That's why it works differently from
id wells the real Mizuhanome creates.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.970
There's no Kaeru.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:41.390
The world looks like an undistorted
version of the real world in the past.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:44.050
Hey, stop staring at me.

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.470
It's creepy.

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:48.050
It's a stare of love.

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:51.180
Stop being rude and finish your breakfast.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.800
Fine.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.350
Right now I remember everything.

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:58.050
I am myself--not some brilliant detective.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.470
Just me.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.180
Oh, it's the case you're working on.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:11.390
They found another
brutally beaten corpse, after all.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:16.010
My family is still alive.

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:21.180
Now, I don't know how long
this bonus time will last,

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:24.140
but if this is the past,

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:27.470
then there's something I can do.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:30.180
Extreme emotional instability?

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:37.220
a finish for boxing gloves
or a similar protective glove,

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:39.470
so it must be the Challenger.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:43.850
And, as before, blood, brain tissue, vomit and
diarrhea, vitreous humor from prior victims--

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.140
Hey. You there.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.050
What are you doing? Sit down.

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:53.550
Who was that?

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:55.930
My subordinate Narihisago.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:57.850
What's gotten into him?

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:05.470
Spill it.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:07.720
Good morning, Momoki.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:10.180
Why did you ignore all my calls?

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.680
I didn't want to get you involved.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:14.430
What? "Involved"?

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:15.850
What are you up to?

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:18.720
Something with no effect on reality.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.550
What does that mean?

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:24.600
Where are we?

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.930
Katsuyama Denshin's home.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:30.050
He's the Challenger. The killer we're pursuing.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.100
Excuse me?!

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:34.300
You go around back.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.800
Hold on! Explain!

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.140
Is there proof?

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.550
I've been here before.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:44.350
Yes?

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:47.050
Good morning.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.470
--Who is it?
--The police.

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:55.430
Mr. Katsuyama Denshin--
no, Mr. Challenger the serial killer,

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:57.180
I came alone.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:05:59.510
Enter.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:08.890
Oh, thanks for your cooperation. Good morning.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:10.720
Good morning.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.760
What business might you have with me?

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.510
It doesn't seem friendly.

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:21.180
Oh, last time I was in a race against
the swat team, so I came in shooting.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.680
I thought I'd take the liberty of a redo.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:26.100
How lucky.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:29.510
For me, and probably for you, too.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:32.140
I came to challenge the Challenger.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:35.800
Fair and square, like a man.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:39.470
"Last time"? We've never met. Isn't that right?

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:42.260
I don't get it. What do you mean?

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:43.260
"Lucky"?

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:46.720
What I'm saying is, this time, let's do it your way.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:48.760
My way.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.600
Here... you mean?

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.350
Or in the arena below us.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:56.550
Didn't you build a little playground down there?

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.550
That space is currently occupied.

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:10.260
Do we need to ring a gong for this?

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:15.220
True combat begins the moment
the fighters acknowledge it.

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:17.510
"Combat"?

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:21.890
You're not doing anything so respectable.

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:27.050
You're a fucking pervert who got off
beating a 14-year-old girl to death.

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:30.510
You're spouting more nonsense. 14-year-old?

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.350
You can ignore that.

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:34.800
You won't live to find out.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.430
I'm sure you want to return
to your arena ASAP. Too bad.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:42.010
I'm fairly strong, you know.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:45.800
Say that after you've defeated a truly strong <i>adult</i>.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.260
Oh, but I have.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:53.890
You killed a pro wrestler
and a martial artist. True.

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:57.720
But someone who even once
beats the shit out of a woman or child

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:01.100
has no right to talk about strength!

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:06.390
What is this nonsense you keep spouting?

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:09.720
Whatever. That's enough chit-chat!

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.550
You won't make me scream.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:23.850
Oh, but you already have.

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.220
Are you really an officer?

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:28.220
You're like a juvenile.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:44.470
You're not going to fight like a man?

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:46.850
I said I'd do this your way.

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:49.890
We're fighting one-on-one, aren't we?

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:12.640
Good. You can still fight.

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:45.640
Hey!

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:49.220
Get up! We're not done! Come at me!

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:10.550
Some "Challenger" you are!

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:13.470
You're not so tough, are you!

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:22.010
All right!

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.390
Narihisago!

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:25.930
You...

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:28.100
What have you done?

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:29.180
I'm calling help.

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:30.510
Don't die on me.

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:32.720
Momoki.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:35.100
Go downstairs first.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.390
There's still... a victim...

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:53.510
Dammit!

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:54.760
Are you okay?

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:56.100
This is the police!

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:01.510
This is horrific.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.470
You're safe now.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.430
Can you tell me your name?

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:08.010
It's okay if you can't.

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:09.640
Can you stand?

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:10.850
Um.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:12.600
Asukai.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:15.510
My name.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:18.550
Asukai Kiki.

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:20.350
Please...

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:22.550
Just let me die.

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:36.220
This name...

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:37.890
Loot at this.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:42.220
Yes?

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:46.850
I'm Narihisago Akihito, Metropolitan Police,
1st Investigation Division.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.430
Come in.

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:55.970
Looks like tonight is the firework festival.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:01.180
Kaeru?

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:05.300
What are...

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.890
What part of the Mizuhanome are you?

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:10.430
Mizu... hanome?

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:13.890
Nevermind. Forgive the intrusion.

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:17.260
It's nice to... meet you, Ms. Asukai Kiki.

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:20.470
What happened to that terrifying man?

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:22.300
The Challenger?

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:23.640
"Challenger"?

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:28.220
Oh, so that's what people were calling him.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.850
Punch me back as hard as you can.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:33.550
Got it?

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:35.720
Unlike normal, this isn't a dream.

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:39.550
If you don't fight back, you will actually die.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.260
Fuck you!

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:44.350
What was that?

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:46.100
I saw the Challenger.

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:47.850
I'm sorry.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:51.300
Could you refrain from speaking his name?

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:54.800
It makes me think about it him.

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:57.930
And then you receive those memories.

00:12:57.930 --> 00:13:00.010
Receive your memories?

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:02.470
What do you...

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:03.970
What's going on?

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:06.470
I don't understand it either.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:12.010
My inner thoughts have always just
broadcast themselves to those around me.

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:15.800
Whether they're words,
memories, or things I imagined.

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:17.720
And dreams, too.

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:21.890
What? How did I know that?

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:26.100
It appears someone else is here, too.

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:40.600
What're those sounds?

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:43.800
The person who kills me tonight.

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:45.220
What do--

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:52.220
Hey, Kiki--

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:55.220
Shit.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:56.760
What the hell?

00:13:56.760 --> 00:13:58.300
The Face-lifter?

00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:00.600
Sonoda Hitoshi! Why is he here?!

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:01.430
Huh?

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:03.850
Hey, hey. How d'ya know my name?

00:14:03.850 --> 00:14:06.010
He's with the police.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:07.600
Huh? The police?

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:11.800
But if you're in her dream,
then aren't you one of us?

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:13.180
Tonight's my turn!

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:15.600
What the fuck are you talking about?

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:17.930
Hey, what is this?

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:22.260
Where'd he go?

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:25.930
He woke up because you made him feel pain.

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:29.800
Though, I always have to die before I wake up.

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:31.470
What are you saying?

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:32.890
What's with this id well?

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:35.600
How are you related to Kaeru?

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:36.800
Id well?

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:39.350
I don't know anyone named Kaeru.

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:40.720
Then where am I?

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:42.970
You're in my dream.

00:14:42.970 --> 00:14:46.640
You're asleep right now, and you entered my dream.

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:51.640
You're awake!

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:54.930
You had me so worried!

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:56.390
Thank goodness.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.180
You've been asleep since the ordeal.

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:00.720
"The ordeal"?

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:04.300
You caught the Challenger two days ago.

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:08.640
Were you having a bad dream?
You were crying out in your sleep.

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:09.850
A dream...

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:12.600
Oh, I'm so relieved!

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:14.850
I'm sorry I worried you.

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:16.890
Hey, Dad.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:21.430
Did you go to the Challenger prepared to die?

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:24.300
Isn't that why you acted weird that morning?

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:27.300
Muku, don't be absurd.

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:29.390
But...

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:32.510
Hey, Dad. Don't die, okay?

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:34.050
This is backwards.

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:36.970
How could I die and leave you two behind?

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:38.220
Narihisago.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:42.850
There are a bunch of things
we have to discuss, but it can wait.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:47.010
It looks like this incident is
going to be labeled self-defense.

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:51.350
Thank you so much. I got
through everything thanks to you.

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:57.260
Come in.

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:05.640
Narihisago from the
1st Investigation Division, was it?

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:08.100
You came to make sure, didn't you.

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:09.470
It wasn't a dream!

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:11.350
No, I guess it was.

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:15.470
So we really did share the same dream.

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:22.970
It was reality--well, whatever "reality" means here.

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:25.300
Forgive me. I'll explain.

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:28.680
I mean, can I share my interpretation with you?

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.890
Two things were happening.

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:33.800
First, I was having the same dream as you.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:38.390
Second, I read your mind during the dream.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:42.640
To be more precise, you entered my dream.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:48.800
And you didn't read my mind--my mind
broadcast itself to you, all on its own.

00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:50.720
I can't say why.

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:55.640
I've never been able to
have a secret all my own.

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.550
We left one thing out.

00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:01.970
A serial killer comes to your dreams.

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.640
To kill you.

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:06.260
That's the only kind of person that comes.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:08.930
Like that man who peels my face off.

00:17:08.930 --> 00:17:10.470
And you.

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:11.720
I'm not like that!

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:14.300
At least, not in this world...

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.430
Ms. Asukai.

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:19.760
I wonder, what is this world?

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:22.100
What is this world to you?

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.600
Is it reality?

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:26.760
Yes. This is not a dream.

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:29.800
No, I don't mean whether it's a dream...

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:34.050
Oh, of course. No point asking
a resident of this world.

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:37.140
Then, what about the Face-lifter,
Sonoda Hitoshi?

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:41.600
He shouted, "Tonight's my turn!"
when he was here.

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:43.220
What did he mean?

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:45.510
He meant that night's dream.

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:50.350
Then, during dreams on other
nights, other serial killers appear?

00:17:50.350 --> 00:17:51.680
--Yes.
--How can you be so calm about this?

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:54.220
--How can you be so calm about this?

00:17:55.850 --> 00:18:01.180
Because various people have been
killing me in my dreams for a long time now.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:05.470
The Challenger and his buddies, right? And others?

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:09.850
And in your dreams, the serial killers
have been murdering you.

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:12.760
Over and over and over and over!

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:16.050
Because in the dreams
they can torment you repeatedly.

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:17.720
Please stop!

00:18:19.100 --> 00:18:21.180
Dammit!

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:22.760
Are you okay?

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:25.100
I'm so sorry.

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:29.720
Once I think about it, I can't
stop it from broadcasting to you.

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:31.430
They're just images.

00:18:31.430 --> 00:18:37.260
But you... Even though it's a dream,
you fully experience it, right?

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:40.100
At first there was only one killer.

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:43.720
But then he started calling others into my dreams...

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.390
This man.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:48.850
Does he have a top hat and a cane?

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:50.220
Yes.

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:53.720
It's makes me want to puke.

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:54.850
Um...

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:59.140
Could you make the doctors
stop me from sleeping?

00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:05.970
Not only am I alternately being killed and
reliving my previous deaths in my dreams,

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:09.300
but the medicines are also
making my head spacey.

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:14.140
Why would the Challenger have
tried to kill you in real life?

00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:18.350
If he did, he wouldn't be able
to kill you in his dreams anymore.

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:23.470
Although the dreams are similar
to reality, they aren't the same.

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:26.850
That man didn't just like to hit people.

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:28.890
He also liked to <i>be </i>hit.

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:31.300
In a dream, you don't actually get injured.

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:35.720
So I believe he kidnapped me
because he got bored with that.

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:42.390
Does it at least ease your misery
a little bit to have the Challenger gone?

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:46.720
I promise to put an end to your misery.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:51.890
I hope you do.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:04.300
You...

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:06.100
How'd you find this place?

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:09.100
Why, we got acquainted in prison!

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:10.220
"Prison"?

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:12.260
I ain't never been to prison!

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:15.260
Ain't even a reason for me to be arrested!

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:18.180
Yeah, not at this stage.

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:22.180
Right! In the end, I'm just
playin' around in a dream.

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:24.300
So I ain't broken no law, right?

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:26.600
Hold up. "At this stage"?

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:28.760
Don't worry about it.

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:33.680
Who the hell are you? Aren't you with us?
With you-know-who?

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:37.800
You mean... the guy with the cane?

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:41.680
I am <i>not </i>one of <i>you</i>.

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:44.680
Did <i>you </i>kill the Challenger?

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.470
Are you here to kill me?

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:50.260
I'm just here to visit. To visit with <i>you</i>.

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:59.850
We're going to have a little chat about
that Kiki girl and the guy with the cane.

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:04.300
Then we'll chat about why you
want to remove people's faces.

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:09.850
And about why you're too chicken-shit
to bring yourself to remove your own face.

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:13.050
We'll have a <i>lovely </i>time.

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:31.930
You don't have to die anymore!

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:36.100
Morning...

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:39.010
Sorry. I didn't mean to startle you.

00:21:42.680 --> 00:21:45.550
Another bad dream, huh.

00:21:45.550 --> 00:21:47.430
Who died?

00:21:48.350 --> 00:21:49.720
Was it me?

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:54.350
I'm not gonna die, you hear me?

00:21:54.350 --> 00:21:58.220
I would never leave you and Muku like that.

00:22:00.050 --> 00:22:01.180
Where <i>is </i>Muku?

00:22:01.180 --> 00:22:04.300
She was tired from going
to the firework festival.

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:06.010
She said she'll come at noon.

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:07.390
Oh.

00:22:07.390 --> 00:22:10.050
Hey, Aki, are you sleeping well at night?

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:14.300
What? No, I haven't slept well in such a long time.

00:22:14.300 --> 00:22:15.640
For how long?

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:17.220
I hardly know anymore.

00:22:17.220 --> 00:22:20.180
Oh, no! Why didn't you tell me?

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:22.220
If only I could have.

00:22:22.220 --> 00:22:26.050
You have to tell me. Sleep is really important.

00:22:26.050 --> 00:22:30.100
Not sleeping is like chipping away at your life.

00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:38.260
I guess that means it's right
to try to help her sleep at night.

00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:39.680
Who do you mean?

00:22:39.680 --> 00:22:42.350
You're the one who needs to sleep, Aki.

00:22:42.350 --> 00:22:45.050
I'm sorry I didn't realize it.

00:22:47.680 --> 00:22:49.180
Aki?

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:55.350
I don't know what happens in your dreams,

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:59.470
but if I die, that's a sign it isn't real.

00:22:59.470 --> 00:23:01.720
All you have to do is wake up.
